NeoSCAD patch to manifold-rust 0.15.0 (crates.io): run the large serial
stages of a boolean in parallel, with output identical to the sequential
code at any thread count (edge-flag and orbit scans, the result
assembly's edge maps, face2tri's writes, the sorts). Test:
crates/geom/tests/parallel_kernels.rs.

Upstream: proposed as branch `neoscad/parallel-booleans`
(commit 1623119) of a fork of larsbrubaker/manifold-rust, on top of its
`main` at 40f20c6 (0.15.0 plus two QuickHull commits that touch none of
these files). This patch is that commit's changes under src/, byte for
byte apart from CRLF line endings; the branch also adds a benchmark
under examples/, which is not vendored.

Apply from the crate root on top of 0002: patch -p1 < this file.
The crate's older sources use CRLF line endings; files this series
adds use LF.
See vendor/README.md ("The parallel boolean patch").

